{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773073308,"nonce":"+9l9jPfOz47eIZWeYVzi4VC7/bo=","title":"Issue scanner misses repos more than 2 levels deep under ~/Main (feedbax not found)","message":"The `discoverRepos()` function in `src/work-scanner.ts` scans `~/Main` at depth=2, meaning it finds repos at `~/Main/X/Y` but not deeper. Feedbax lives at `~/Main/10 Projects/10 PhD/20 Feedbax/feedbax` (4 levels deep) and is never registered.\n\n## Symptoms\n\n- Clicking an issue pill on a feedbax auth request navigates to the Issues tab but shows \"Failed to load issue detail\"\n- `GET /api/issues/find/20a4b8c` returns `{\"error\":\"issue not found in any scanned repo\"}`\n- `GET /api/issues` returns only `[\"dotfiles\", \"mll-bio\"]`\n\n## Root cause\n\n`scanDirForRepos(~/Main, depth=2)` recursively descends at most 2 levels. `mll-bio` at depth 2 (`~/Main/15 WWW/mll.bio`) is found; feedbax at depth 4 is not.\n\n## Fix options\n\n1. **Read `repos.toml`**: The monorepo at `~/Main` has `/.projects/repos.toml` listing all repo paths explicitly. Mandible could read this file and register those repos directly — no scanning needed, no depth limit.\n2. **Increase scan depth**: Change depth=2 to depth=4 or depth=5 for `~/Main`. Risks: slower startup, accidentally picking up nested `.git` dirs inside repos.\n3. **Explicit config**: Add a `extra_repo_roots` config field for repos that fall outside the auto-scan range.\n\nOption 1 (repos.toml integration) is likely the cleanest — the file already exists and is maintained.","files":null}]}